{
  "slug": "artist:noisecontrollers",
  "name": "Noisecontrollers",
  "editorial_article": "Bas Oskam, the Dutch producer behind the Noisecontrollers project, began his career in 2005 alongside Arjan Terpstra, establishing himself as a pioneer of technical and melodic hardstyle. The duo initially emulated the sound of the group Donkey Rollers, a move that helped secure their early signing to Fusion Records. Oskam’s production approach evolved significantly after collaborative sessions with Headhunterz and Wildstylez at the Scantraxx studios, which resulted in the influential 2009 track \"Tonight.\" In 2010, Oskam took a more central role in studio operations, leading to the creation of the anthem \"CTRL.ALT.DEL\" for In Qontrol, where he debuted a deep, pitch-shifted kick drum technique he would utilize for years. Following Terpstra’s departure in 2013, Oskam continued as a solo act, exploring diverse sounds including big room house and dubstep on the collaboration \"Get Loose\" with Showtek. Throughout his career, he has founded several labels, including Digital:Age, Spirit of Hardstyle, and contributed to the Art of Creation collective. Oskam’s 2012 debut studio album, E=Nc² (The Science Of Hardstyle), remains a notable body of work in the genre, distinct for its conceptual focus on science.",
